  "notes": [
    "the 2.0 case is written to --text-scale directly, which is the same root the Large control moves, so it stands for a visitor who asks the browser for 200 percent text; the app itself offers Small, Medium and Large only.",
    "the sweep compares each element with itself across one page load: every element keeps a stamp and an ancestry line, so an element that kept a pixel size cannot hide behind a different element count, and a DOM node React reused for different markup is counted in \"remodelled\" instead of being compared with itself."
